00:31:15.940 --> 00:31:17.260
But I'll just ask you two or three now.

00:31:17.260 --> 00:31:18.656
I thought this was really interesting,

00:31:18.656 --> 00:31:21.830
and I got a lot of this type of question.

00:31:21.830 --> 00:31:26.100
What is the acceptable level
of risk in terms of disease

00:31:26.100 --> 00:31:27.892
and death that we're willing to accept

00:31:27.892 --> 00:31:30.970
in order to have a normally
functioning society

00:31:30.970 --> 00:31:32.223
and healthy economy?

00:31:33.400 --> 00:31:35.230
- Well, I would ask you
to think about what we do

00:31:35.230 --> 00:31:37.410
when it comes to mining safety,

00:31:37.410 --> 00:31:38.852
or other dangerous occupations

00:31:38.852 --> 00:31:40.920
like whether we equip our police

00:31:40.920 --> 00:31:43.630
with bulletproof vests, for example.

00:31:43.630 --> 00:31:46.950
We spend money in a preventive
way to prevent deaths

00:31:46.950 --> 00:31:49.470
and hazardous occupations all the time.

00:31:49.470 --> 00:31:51.280
Now, we don't spend limitlessly,

00:31:51.280 --> 00:31:53.740
we don't equip each police officer,

00:31:53.740 --> 00:31:56.900
we expect people to
take some risk of death.

00:31:56.900 --> 00:32:00.098
We don't spend limitlessly
even to secure our highways.

00:32:00.098 --> 00:32:02.016
Not every highway is a divided highway,

00:32:02.016 --> 00:32:05.610
which we know is safer,
because it would cost too much.

00:32:05.610 --> 00:32:07.290
So there's some calculation we make

00:32:07.290 --> 00:32:09.321
about how much money
we're willing to spend

00:32:09.321 --> 00:32:11.066
in order to save lives.

00:32:11.066 --> 00:32:12.600
And what you have to understand

00:32:12.600 --> 00:32:14.688
in this case is that we're
dealing with a threat.

00:32:14.688 --> 00:32:17.010
And instantly death is expensive too,

00:32:17.010 --> 00:32:17.877
like all these people dying

00:32:17.877 --> 00:32:21.290
and consuming healthcare is expensive.

00:32:21.290 --> 00:32:25.030
So, preventing those death
saves us money as well.

00:32:25.030 --> 00:32:27.880
I acknowledge as most experts do,

00:32:27.880 --> 00:32:31.450
that taking our economy
is a devastating thing.

00:32:31.450 --> 00:32:35.880
But I would suggest that if
people started dying like flies,

00:32:35.880 --> 00:32:38.310
if 300,000 Americans started dying,

00:32:38.310 --> 00:32:40.640
our economy would have tanked anyway.

00:32:40.640 --> 00:32:44.840
So the problem again, is not that 300,000

00:32:44.840 --> 00:32:47.940
extra Americans are gonna
die, although that's not good.

00:32:47.940 --> 00:32:51.250
It's that they're gonna
die very compressed.

00:32:51.250 --> 00:32:53.560
We're not just spreading them out.

00:32:53.560 --> 00:32:57.220
And so that's a devastating
blow to our society

00:32:57.220 --> 00:32:58.053
no matter what.

00:32:58.053 --> 00:33:00.450
So I guess, I would say that

00:33:00.450 --> 00:33:03.670
